<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zhou Daguan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. <a href="/years/1296">1296</a>–<a href="/years/1297">1297</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zhou Daguan was a Chinese official of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan dynasty</a> who accompanied an embassy sent by Temür Khan to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angkor">Angkor</a> in 1296–1297. His account of the visit, A Record of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambodia">Cambodia</a>, describes the city, its temples, royal processions, trade, customs and daily life. It is the only surviving eyewitness description of Angkor at the height of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-empire">Khmer Empire</a>.</p></div>
